# data/fibo_live/v1/events.jsonl is append-only and every line carries its
# own timestamp, so line order is not semantically load-bearing -- a
# union merge (keep both sides' lines, never asking for manual conflict
# resolution) is safe here. This is the fix for BUGS.md's evening-job
# git-divergence entry: GitHub Actions (morning job) and this laptop
# (evening job) are two independent writers to the same file, so
# diverging branches are the normal state, not an error -- see
# src/fibo_live/git_sync.py's pull_before_appending docstring.
# fibo_live/eventlog.py's read_events() also dedupes by event_id as
# cheap insurance against a line appearing on both sides of a merge.
data/fibo_live/v1/*.jsonl merge=union
